  "term": "lateral hypothalamus",
  "definition": "The lateral hypothalamus is a part of the hypothalamus identified by its position between nearby fiber tracts and adjacent brain regions. It includes the lateral hypothalamic nucleus, the tuberomammillary nucleus, the lateral tuberal nuclei, and fibers of the medial forebrain bundle.",
